WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.352 --> 00:00:03.650
- He's the son of divorced
immigrant parents.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:06.868
When he was nine, he sold
newspapers and Christmas cards

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.468
to support his family.

00:00:08.468 --> 00:00:11.988
Today he's worth almost
three billion dollars.

00:00:11.988 --> 00:00:13.326
He's John Paul DeJoria,

00:00:13.326 --> 00:00:16.826
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:18.821 --> 00:00:21.669
- Well, you get there through
one, believing in yourself.

00:00:21.669 --> 00:00:23.597
As you know so well, when we started,

00:00:23.597 --> 00:00:27.279
we had $700, made it day to day barely,

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:30.367
but we believed what we did
was the very, very best.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.590
And it goes on the premise if you realize

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.365
that you're going to run
across a lot of rejection.

00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:37.061
I say this time in and time out,

00:00:37.061 --> 00:00:38.782
be prepared for the rejection.

00:00:38.782 --> 00:00:40.062
No matter how bad it is,

00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:42.686
don't let it overcome
you or influence you.

00:00:42.686 --> 00:00:45.478
Keep on going towards what
you want to do no matter what,

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.909
no matter whether your
bills are paid, not paid,

00:00:47.909 --> 00:00:50.102
someone says no a thousand times.

00:00:50.102 --> 00:00:53.126
Again, go back to be as
enthusiastic on door number 100

00:00:53.126 --> 00:00:55.029
as you were on door number one.

00:00:55.029 --> 00:00:56.518
But believe in yourself,

00:00:56.518 --> 00:00:58.110
and it's really all about knowing

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.983
you have a great service
or a great product

00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:03.357
that will put you in the reorder business.

00:01:03.357 --> 00:01:04.741
So you're never selling,

00:01:04.741 --> 00:01:06.598
you're trying to get
it in someone's hands,

00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:08.325
whether it's a service or a product,

00:01:08.325 --> 00:01:09.501
knowing it's so darn good

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.973
that they're going to
want to order it again

00:01:10.973 --> 00:01:12.886
or tell a friend about it to order.

00:01:12.886 --> 00:01:14.358
And that's the real secret there.

00:01:14.358 --> 00:01:16.038
- I quit almost twice in my life,

00:01:16.038 --> 00:01:18.886
and when you're down and
out, it's not an easy thing.

00:01:18.886 --> 00:01:21.749
The first time I was
homeless I was 23 years old.

00:01:21.749 --> 00:01:24.413
Second time was when I started
John Paul Mitchell Systems

00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:25.998
and I was in my 30s.

00:01:25.998 --> 00:01:28.014
I started thinking how bad things are,

00:01:28.014 --> 00:01:29.421
and oh my God, things are bad.

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:32.037
How do I exist in this bad situation?

00:01:32.037 --> 00:01:33.922
I looked at "How do I get out of it?"

00:01:33.922 --> 00:01:35.810
One time, I had no money.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.730
I had a car that had a broken radiator,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.564
had to keep on putting water in it,

00:01:39.564 --> 00:01:42.731
but I would go around
collecting old soda pop bottles,

00:01:42.731 --> 00:01:44.642
take them in, two cents for a little one,

00:01:44.642 --> 00:01:45.826
five cents for a big one,

00:01:45.826 --> 00:01:48.594
get some money and look for part-time jobs

00:01:48.594 --> 00:01:50.507
no matter what they paid.

00:01:50.507 --> 00:01:51.970
I wanted to get out of it.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:52.828
I didn't want to be,

00:01:52.828 --> 00:01:55.058
okay, I'm going to have to
stay this way for awhile,

00:01:55.058 --> 00:01:56.131
how do I survive?

00:01:56.131 --> 00:01:58.042
I look at how I got out of it.

00:01:58.042 --> 00:02:00.085
And by gosh, you can get out of it.

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:01.562
America does work.

00:02:01.562 --> 00:02:03.538
You just have to do something.

00:02:03.538 --> 00:02:05.351
It's the combination of one the product,

00:02:05.351 --> 00:02:07.503
but you could also have the
best product in the world,

00:02:07.503 --> 00:02:10.095
but unless you tell people
about it, get them to use it,

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:11.458
it's just going to sit there.

00:02:11.458 --> 00:02:13.095
So it's a combination
of a couple of things.

00:02:13.095 --> 00:02:15.223
One, that product was exceptional.

00:02:15.223 --> 00:02:17.160
Same with Patrón Tequilas, Paul Mitchell

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.975
or John Paul Pet, exceptional product,

00:02:19.975 --> 00:02:23.856
but then one must do what
those that maybe aren't quite

00:02:23.856 --> 00:02:26.567
as successful don't want
to do, whatever it takes.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:29.551
Work seven days a week from
early morning to late at night.

00:02:29.551 --> 00:02:30.975
A lot of rejection comes your way.

00:02:30.975 --> 00:02:32.671
Overcome that rejection.

00:02:32.671 --> 00:02:34.591
And know that what you have is so good

00:02:34.591 --> 00:02:37.271
eventually you'll get through it.

00:02:37.271 --> 00:02:38.991
Eventually, you get in
the reorder business.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:42.447
Successful people do the
things unsuccessful people

00:02:42.447 --> 00:02:45.447
don't want to do or have a very
difficult time doing, guys,

00:02:45.447 --> 00:02:46.687
very difficult time.

00:02:46.687 --> 00:02:49.755
And that is keeping yourself going

00:02:49.755 --> 00:02:51.186
when nothing's working,

00:02:51.186 --> 00:02:55.082
when everyone else is
saying, "No, no, no, no, no."

00:02:55.082 --> 00:02:58.498
First thing would be in your category

00:02:58.498 --> 00:03:01.898
make it the best you possibly can,

00:03:01.898 --> 00:03:05.250
so when the end result is
the consumer is tasting it

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.105
is it something they want to get again.

00:03:07.105 --> 00:03:08.434
That's number one.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:10.674
Second thing is you have a story

00:03:10.674 --> 00:03:13.674
or an excitement behind it which is true.

00:03:13.674 --> 00:03:15.297
We did that with Patrón for example.

00:03:15.297 --> 00:03:19.050
We had a tequila-tasting test back in 1989

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.506
at Spago's Restaurant and
we just won hands down.

00:03:21.506 --> 00:03:24.202
So there was some validity
not just from taste

00:03:24.202 --> 00:03:25.778
but from what was going on.

00:03:25.778 --> 00:03:27.954
But in any product, let's
say you want to start

00:03:27.954 --> 00:03:31.114
an envelope company, Steve,
a tequila company, anything.

00:03:31.114 --> 00:03:35.322
You have to know yourself
that it's the best you can do.

00:03:35.322 --> 00:03:38.970
And then you have to be
willing to tell enough people

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.689
until enough people say yes.

00:03:40.689 --> 00:03:44.197
Once they say, you have to
put your personality into it.

00:03:44.197 --> 00:03:45.485
Go by and thank them.

00:03:45.485 --> 00:03:46.725
Make sure it's going well.

00:03:46.725 --> 00:03:48.549
A lot of people just shot
something out to get,

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:50.533
"Can I get 1,000 customers?"

00:03:50.533 --> 00:03:52.237
where they have the first 50 or 100

00:03:52.237 --> 00:03:53.669
and don't pay attention to them.

00:03:53.669 --> 00:03:56.101
You must pay attention
to your first customers

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:57.525
unreal attention.

00:03:57.525 --> 00:03:59.213
It's easier to keep somebody than it is

00:03:59.213 --> 00:04:00.558
to just try to get somebody new.

00:04:00.558 --> 00:04:02.989
Let's do the best we
can with what we have.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:05.318
See, we want to live in the now.

00:04:05.318 --> 00:04:08.477
And usually when you're down
and out or having difficulties,

00:04:08.477 --> 00:04:10.653
your mind is working very fast.

00:04:10.653 --> 00:04:13.610
Not your brain, your mind
is working very fast.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.293
And it's working an awful
lot of nows from the past.

00:04:16.293 --> 00:04:18.822
So a lot of experiences
from the past and worries of

00:04:18.822 --> 00:04:21.255
what may happen in the future
are going through your mind.

00:04:21.255 --> 00:04:22.799
Well, if you can eliminate that by saying,

00:04:22.799 --> 00:04:25.135
"Okay, there's nothing
to do about the past.

00:04:25.135 --> 00:04:25.968
That's done.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.072
Yesterday's newspapers.

00:04:27.072 --> 00:04:28.095
Can't change them.

00:04:28.095 --> 00:04:30.377
And who knows for sure what's
going to happen in the future?

00:04:30.377 --> 00:04:31.406
Let's be here right now.

00:04:31.406 --> 00:04:34.678
Take what resources we have
right now, act upon them,

00:04:34.678 --> 00:04:36.549
and act towards a good future goal."

00:04:36.549 --> 00:04:38.939
- So you are actually
going along the street

00:04:38.939 --> 00:04:42.261
trading in, y'know, bottles
to get a nickel a piece.

00:04:42.261 --> 00:04:45.525
- Oh, yeah, in those days,
actually it's the second time

00:04:45.525 --> 00:04:46.867
I was homeless, okay?

00:04:46.867 --> 00:04:47.700
But in those days,

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.685
you got two cents for a little pop bottle,

00:04:49.685 --> 00:04:50.837
five cents for a big one.

00:04:50.837 --> 00:04:53.405
And every grocery store
and every liquor store,

00:04:53.405 --> 00:04:55.293
you would just bring them to
and they give you the money.

00:04:55.293 --> 00:04:56.837
And, y'know, you do what
you have to do to exist

00:04:56.837 --> 00:04:58.709
if times are lean.

00:04:58.709 --> 00:05:01.733
But at least this nation
affords us that opportunity.

00:05:01.733 --> 00:05:02.845
If you now where you're at,

00:05:02.845 --> 00:05:04.925
well, how can I best make it to survive?

00:05:04.925 --> 00:05:06.526
Not oh poor me.

00:05:06.526 --> 00:05:10.100
How do I entrench myself
for longterm survival is

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.772
how to I survive right now,
get myself to the next step.

00:05:12.772 --> 00:05:14.660
That's the attitude you have to have.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.668
First starters, we know we
have a darn good product.

00:05:16.668 --> 00:05:19.396
But if we take the time
with ourselves and our staff

00:05:19.396 --> 00:05:22.532
to go there and tell them
all the ways to use it

00:05:22.532 --> 00:05:24.620
and reassure them not
only is it a good product

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.876
but here's how you use it to
create a good salon experience

00:05:27.876 --> 00:05:30.076
or the consumer when you take it home

00:05:30.076 --> 00:05:32.636
to keep your hair the
same in between visits,

00:05:32.636 --> 00:05:35.004
you fill a need in the market place.

00:05:35.004 --> 00:05:37.559
One, there's the need, of
course, to buy a product

00:05:37.559 --> 00:05:38.932
or another product.

00:05:38.932 --> 00:05:41.388
But the next one is you
must constantly remind them

00:05:41.388 --> 00:05:44.044
how to use it properly, which
makes you a little different.

00:05:44.044 --> 00:05:46.420
Now granted, maybe there's
another one to use the same way,

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.170
but nobody told them.

00:05:49.008 --> 00:05:50.303
We're amazed at times when people

00:05:50.303 --> 00:05:52.255
are using our finest products

00:05:52.255 --> 00:05:54.847
and didn't know there's
other ways to use it also.

00:05:54.847 --> 00:05:55.811
It's through education.

00:05:55.811 --> 00:05:57.975
You must constantly
reinforce the education

00:05:57.975 --> 00:05:58.935
and why it's so good.

00:05:58.935 --> 00:06:00.919
I don't care what you have in life,

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:02.535
no matter where you are in your life,

00:06:02.535 --> 00:06:06.098
there always be somebody that
needs it more than you do.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:08.248
So whatever you give,
as little as it might be

00:06:08.248 --> 00:06:10.023
or whether if it's your own self,

00:06:10.023 --> 00:06:13.247
I know in my early 20s, I
didn't have a lot of money,

00:06:13.247 --> 00:06:16.231
but at Thanksgiving and Christmas,

00:06:16.231 --> 00:06:19.007
I'd be in Griffith Park in
the line at the feed-in.

00:06:19.007 --> 00:06:21.591
I'd be feeding people that
came in the lines there.

00:06:21.591 --> 00:06:23.002
I was they're at the feed-in.

00:06:23.002 --> 00:06:24.034
I could serve really good.

00:06:24.034 --> 00:06:25.746
I could cut a turkey so cold, man.

00:06:25.746 --> 00:06:26.618
I got really good at that.

00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:28.066
I was a good server.

00:06:28.066 --> 00:06:31.770
It made me feel good, because
I was part of giving back.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:34.154
As you are a part of giving
back, it opens you up.

00:06:34.154 --> 00:06:37.146
It opens you, the human
being, up in a huge way.

00:06:37.146 --> 00:06:40.586
Your soul, the entity
inside of you, opens up.

00:06:40.586 --> 00:06:41.666
It's the most amazing thing.

00:06:41.666 --> 00:06:44.731
It's not about "poor
me, me, me, me, poor me,

00:06:44.731 --> 00:06:46.770
"I'm going to get my little
quarter over here, poor me."

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.906
It's about "Hey, I'm going to give.

00:06:48.906 --> 00:06:49.803
"I may not have any money,

00:06:49.803 --> 00:06:51.106
"but I'm going to open that door for you."

00:06:51.106 --> 00:06:51.940
You need an helping hand.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.107
I'm going to be there for you.

00:06:53.107 --> 00:06:54.570
I'm going to lend a helping hand.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.402
Your whole being opens up
when things like this happen.

00:06:57.402 --> 00:07:00.915
When we hire people at Patrón
or John Paul Mitchell Systems,

00:07:00.915 --> 00:07:03.691
the people we hire do more than one thing.

00:07:03.691 --> 00:07:07.543
We purposely give someone
the responsibility

00:07:07.543 --> 00:07:09.064
of several positions.

00:07:09.064 --> 00:07:11.079
They're paid extremely well.

00:07:11.079 --> 00:07:12.967
We take more than good care of them,

00:07:12.967 --> 00:07:15.152
but it gives them the
opportunity to be in something

00:07:15.152 --> 00:07:16.831
that if times are every tough,

00:07:16.831 --> 00:07:18.959
you don't have to eliminate anybody.

00:07:18.959 --> 00:07:21.256
They can migrate into a variety of things,

00:07:21.256 --> 00:07:23.615
because they're already doing it.

00:07:23.615 --> 00:07:25.616
Now as business thinks about this

00:07:25.616 --> 00:07:27.951
and they start hiring
people from beginning

00:07:27.951 --> 00:07:29.568
with fewer moving parts.

00:07:29.568 --> 00:07:32.087
We probably have one-fourth
the amount of staff

00:07:32.087 --> 00:07:33.975
that our competitors have,

00:07:33.975 --> 00:07:36.527
y'know, per capita and per
what we do in business.

00:07:36.527 --> 00:07:39.663
But we hire where you
do more than one thing.

00:07:39.663 --> 00:07:40.847
In fact, I think it's one of the things

00:07:40.847 --> 00:07:42.648
that's going to make America great.

00:07:42.648 --> 00:07:45.311
It made America great in the past.

00:07:45.311 --> 00:07:47.347
It hasn't been quite as
great as it could be,

00:07:47.347 --> 00:07:48.680
but it will be in the future.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.679
Where people instead of
getting one job to do,

00:07:50.679 --> 00:07:51.935
one thing all the time,

00:07:51.935 --> 00:07:54.253
that they draw it out
because it gets so boring,

00:07:54.253 --> 00:07:56.109
they two or three things.

00:07:56.109 --> 00:07:57.669
All of a sudden, they're
happy what they're doing.

00:07:57.669 --> 00:08:00.021
They're excited about it
and their day is full.

00:08:00.021 --> 00:08:04.317
Longterm entrepreneurship
is liking what you do,

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:07.454
who you do it with and who you do it for.

00:08:07.454 --> 00:08:09.285
If you're not having fun,

00:08:09.285 --> 00:08:11.549
then you're only in business
to makes some money.

00:08:11.549 --> 00:08:12.429
I still work.

00:08:12.429 --> 00:08:15.037
I work every single day,
but I love what I do,

00:08:15.037 --> 00:08:15.870
so I have fun.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.341
So it became a lifestyle.

00:08:17.341 --> 00:08:19.421
When you're working, it becomes work.

00:08:19.421 --> 00:08:20.381
It's not fun.

00:08:20.381 --> 00:08:22.477
When you're working because
part of your lifestyle,

00:08:22.477 --> 00:08:23.757
because you like it, it's fun.

00:08:23.757 --> 00:08:25.597
I look forward to calling on salons.

00:08:25.597 --> 00:08:27.557
I look forward to walking in some places

00:08:27.557 --> 00:08:29.682
and say, "Thank you for
using Paul Mitchell."

00:08:29.682 --> 00:08:33.123
I look forward to walking
into a cocktail lounge.

00:08:33.123 --> 00:08:34.832
"Wow, thank you for having
Patrón on the menu."

00:08:34.832 --> 00:08:36.608
To people in the hip-hop industry,

00:08:36.608 --> 00:08:38.160
"Thank you for singing about Patrón."

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.209
In the country-western industry,

00:08:39.209 --> 00:08:40.392
"Thank you for doing thing."

00:08:40.392 --> 00:08:42.285
In other words, I like it so much

00:08:42.285 --> 00:08:45.598
that I appreciate so much also
the people that like it too.

00:08:45.598 --> 00:08:47.614
It's a lifestyle, and it's a good one.

00:08:47.614 --> 00:08:51.004
So if an entrepreneur can make
a lifestyle that they like

00:08:51.004 --> 00:08:52.651
with the people they want to deal with

00:08:52.651 --> 00:08:53.587
part of their business,

00:08:53.587 --> 00:08:55.445
it'll be longterm and it will prosper,

00:08:55.445 --> 00:08:57.147
because you are having fun.

00:08:57.147 --> 00:08:59.065
And everyone wants to have fun.

00:08:59.065 --> 00:08:59.898
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:08:59.898 --> 00:09:03.242
I made this video because
Moe Modern asked me too.

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:05.034
So if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:09:05.034 --> 00:09:07.146
to profile next, leave
it in the comments below,

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:08.626
and I'll see what I can do.

00:09:08.626 --> 00:09:11.448
I'd also love to know
which of the 10 rules

00:09:11.448 --> 00:09:12.849
you feel most connected to,

00:09:12.849 --> 00:09:14.064
which helped you the most.

00:09:14.064 --> 00:09:15.185
Leave it in the comments below.

00:09:15.185 --> 00:09:16.600
I'm going to join the discussion.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:17.904
Thanks again for watching.

00:09:17.904 --> 00:09:21.487
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

